<title>BELGIUM: EU economic forecasts delayed.</title>
<headline>EU economic forecasts delayed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday that release of its economic forecasts for 1997 had been delayed beyond the scheduled 0900 GMT publication time.</p>
<p>Commission officials said commissioners were still discussing the forecasts at their regular weekly meeting and that the figures would be released afterwards.</p>
<p>The figures are expected to show all 15 EU countries except Italy and Greece meeting Maastricht Treaty criteria for Economic and Monetary Union.</p>
</text>
